---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { site } from "../lib/site";
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy"
  description="Dunlin does not collect analytics, telemetry, or accounts. The website is static and sets no cookies."
  eyebrow="Legal · Privacy"
>
  <h2>Short version</h2>
  <p>
    Dunlin does not collect analytics, telemetry, or personal data. There is no
    account and no sign in. The website is static and sets no cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    The site is a static marketing page. Fonts are self hosted. There is no
    third party analytics, advertising, or tracking script. The hosting provider
    may keep standard access logs (IP address, user agent, requested URL) for
    security and operations. Those logs are controlled by the host, not by
    Dunlin.
  </p>

  <h2>Downloads</h2>
  <p>
    Downloads are served by GitHub Releases. GitHub may process request data
    under its own privacy policy. Dunlin does not receive a notification when
    you download a release.
  </p>

  <h2>The app</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Projects, sessions, transcripts and settings are stored locally in SQLite.
    </li>
    <li>No prompt, tool payload, or project file is sent to Dunlin servers.</li>
    <li>
      The harness you choose runs as a local child process. Its own privacy
      policy and network behavior apply.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you connect a relay, files and sessions go only to the server you run.
      The relay operator controls that data.
    </li>
    <li>Relay tokens are stored in the macOS Keychain.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or corrections: open an issue at
    <a href={site.github} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      {site.github.replace("https://", "")}
    </a>
    .
  </p>
</Legal>
